   "stem": {
      "text": "The length \\( L(t) \\) and the width \\( W(t) \\) of a rectangle, both measured in centimeters, are differentiable functions of time \\( t \\), measured in seconds. The table gives values of \\( L \\), \\( W \\), and their derivatives at selected times. \\[ \\begin{array}{c|cccc} t & 0 & 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ \\hline L(t) & 10 & 12 & 15 & 16 \\\\ L'(t) & 3 & 2 & 4 & 1 \\\\ W(t) & 6 & 5 & 4 & 3 \\\\ W'(t) & -1 & -1 & -2 & -1 \\end{array} \\]"
   },
   "skills": [
      "BC-SKL-02037",
      "BC-SKL-02041",
      "BC-SKL-02017"
   ],
   "parts": [
      {
         "id": "a",
         "prompt": "The area of the rectangle is \\( A(t) = L(t)\\,W(t) \\). Find \\( A'(2) \\). Show the work that leads to your answer.",
         "setup_required": false,
         "answer_latex": "A'(2) = -14",
         "worked_solution": [
            {
               "text": "Product rule.",
               "latex": "A'(t) = L'(t)\\,W(t) + L(t)\\,W'(t)"
            },
            {
               "text": "Substitute the values at t = 2.",
               "latex": "A'(2) = 4 \\cdot 4 + 15 \\cdot (-2) = -14"
            }
         ],
         "points": [
            {
               "point_id": "a1",
               "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99022",
               "skills": [
                  "BC-SKL-02037"
