                  "expected": "-14",
                  "up_to_constant": false,
                  "variable": "t"
               }
            }
         ]
      },
      {
         "id": "b",
         "prompt": "Let \\( r(t) = \\dfrac{L(t)}{W(t)} \\) and \\( s(t) = \\dfrac{W(t)}{L(t)} \\). Find \\( r'(1) \\) and \\( s'(1) \\).",
         "setup_required": false,
         "answer_latex": "r'(1) = \\frac{22}{25}, \\quad s'(1) = -\\frac{11}{72}",
         "worked_solution": [
            {
               "text": "Quotient rule for r at t = 1.",
               "latex": "r'(1) = \\frac{L'(1)\\,W(1) - L(1)\\,W'(1)}{\\left[ W(1) \\right]^{2}} = \\frac{2 \\cdot 5 - 12 \\cdot (-1)}{25} = \\frac{22}{25}"
            },
            {
               "text": "Quotient rule for s at t = 1.",
               "latex": "s'(1) = \\frac{W'(1)\\,L(1) - W(1)\\,L'(1)}{\\left[ L(1) \\right]^{2}} = \\frac{(-1) \\cdot 12 - 5 \\cdot 2}{144} = -\\frac{11}{72}"
            }
