      {
         "id": "d",
         "prompt": "The perimeter of the rectangle is \\( P(t) = 2L(t) + 2W(t) \\). Let \\( Q(t) = \\dfrac{A(t)}{P(t)} \\). Find \\( P'(2) \\) and \\( Q'(2) \\).",
         "setup_required": false,
         "answer_latex": "P'(2) = 4, \\quad Q'(2) = -\\frac{193}{361}",
         "worked_solution": [
            {
               "text": "Differentiate the perimeter.",
               "latex": "P'(2) = 2L'(2) + 2W'(2) = 2 \\cdot 4 + 2 \\cdot (-2) = 4"
            },
            {
               "text": "Values at t = 2, with A'(2) from part (a).",
               "latex": "A(2) = 60, \\quad A'(2) = -14, \\quad P(2) = 38"
